  [PASS] RD3-e THE EXACT OBSTRUCTION, NAMED AND EXHIBITED (the D44f lesson at reception grain): the reception STATE is order-blind — the two orders give byte-identical sigma_A and sigma_B (props {A/V0/0, B/V0/1}, resolved empty, superseded empty, created empty, holdings {V0}) — but the ARBITRATION MENU is not. Under ORD-1 the delivery register-links A to B, so B's proposal is received IN THE CAUSAL FUTURE of A's: the two proposals are comparable, no conflict edge forms, the view carries TWO singleton components and each actor's menu is one self-arbitration at weight 1/4. Under ORD-2 the proposals are concurrent: ONE two-element conflicting component, each actor's menu is TWO pair-arbitrations at weight 1/8 (the K1 winner split). THE ORDER-DETERMINED DATUM, named exactly: the causal COMPARABILITY of the two proposal receptions — equivalently the conflict-edge structure of the live component — which the reception state does not carry and the menu and its prices do  (both orders fully admissible; sigma_A and sigma_B identical across the orders; components 1+1 vs 2; menus 1 x 1/4 vs 2 x 1/8 per actor)
